# Do exactly what was asked

The user's words are the whole change. Do that change. Stop.

If the user names a word to remove, remove that word. Leave the rest of the phrase as it was.

Do not replace the phrase with a product name, a sidebar label, a style-guide form, or a name that seems more correct. Do not rename, rephrase, or "fix" anything the user did not name in that message.

```
Wrong: The user says remove the word Single from the title "Single container". The title becomes "Container as a service".
Right: The title becomes "Container".
```

A later message is a new instruction. It does not expand the previous one.
